WEBVTT - GlanceTrail Demo Captions

00:00.000 --> 00:07.500
When you practice a presentation, notes help you remember your words—but they pull your eyes out of the room.

00:07.500 --> 00:15.000
GlanceTrail turns the room itself into a memory path so you can rehearse with your eyes up.

00:15.000 --> 00:25.000
Built for SPECS, GlanceTrail places three pitch beats directly in front of you.

00:25.000 --> 00:35.000
About one meter away, Problem sits on the left, Proof in the center, and Ask on the right.

00:35.000 --> 00:45.000
During your first rehearsal, each beacon gives you a short cue, with deeper detail available on demand with a simple pinch.

00:45.000 --> 00:55.000
Advancing with the large Continue button folds the idea into a warm memory beacon and awakens the next beat.

00:55.000 --> 01:05.000
We advance through Proof and Ask.

01:05.000 --> 01:15.000
Once you finish Ask, the three locations connect into one visible trail, linking your ideas together in physical space.

01:15.000 --> 01:25.000
Now comes the transformation. On your second rehearsal, the sentences vanish. Only spatial symbols remain.

01:25.000 --> 01:35.000
If you hesitate, a quick pinch on the rescue hint reveals your cue for two seconds before fading away.

01:35.000 --> 01:50.000
If you turn away, an edge indicator gently points you back. You aren't reciting paragraphs—you're walking a path.

01:50.000 --> 02:00.000
Under the hood, GlanceTrail is built with the Spectacles Interaction Kit and UI Kit, using an explicit state controller.

02:00.000 --> 02:10.000
Seven automated Node tests cover every done criterion and the duplicate-input seam; the full two-pass flow was also verified in native Interactive Preview.

02:10.000 --> 02:25.000
This belongs on glasses because it keeps your hands free, your posture natural, and your eyes connected with your audience. GlanceTrail: Rehearse the path, not the paragraph.

